; Entity handler: spitting plant of room 14, position and hit test
;
; The three magenta plants of "Hidden garden" (room 14): handler of room object kind 12 (#R$B028, behaviour block
; #R$953D). A plant stays where it is, opens its head and spits two seeds, one flying up and left and one up and right
; (#R$B74B), every 120 frames; touching a plant kills the monk. Entity handlers are not called: the slot walker
; #R$A5E9 sets SP to a slot of #R$C100 and RETs, so the handler is entered with SP at slot+2 and finds its state on the
; stack.
; .
; Slot (the layout of the room enemies made by #R$89ED): +2 and +4 words not used, +6 word x and +8 word y (8.8, high
; bytes in 2-pixel units; x is a multiple of 4), +$A byte not used and +$B byte the reload of the spit countdown (both
; $78), +$C word hit box offset (y, x), +$E word hit box far corner (y, x), +$10 pointer to the sprite block (attribute,
; height, width, two frames), +$12 byte spit countdown (the other byte of the word is not used here), +$14 byte frame
; and +$15 number of frames (2).
; .
; This routine stores the position as the start position of the seeds (SPAWN_POSITION), makes the position of the draw
; command (#R$ACD1: y, x/4), keeps +$B in A', and tests the hit box against the monk with #R$A85F, with #R$B687 as the
; continuation (carry set when the boxes overlap).
;
; SP Slot address + 2 (the handler word was popped by the RET that entered the routine)
@label=UpdatePlant
c$B665 POP BC        ; +2, not used
 $B666 POP BC        ; +4, not used
 $B667 POP HL        ; x word
 $B668 LD D,H        ; D = x
 $B669 POP HL        ; y word
 $B66A LD E,H        ; E = y
 $B66B LD H,D        ;
 $B66C LD L,E        ; HL = x (H) and y (L), 2-pixel units
 $B66D LD ($5DFE),HL ; start position of the seeds: SPAWN_POSITION
 $B670 SRA H         ; x / 4 = byte column
 $B672 SRA H         ;
 $B674 LD ($ACD3),HL ; position of the draw command: y, byte column
 $B677 POP AF        ; +$A and +$B: A = the reload of the spit countdown
 $B678 EX AF,AF'     ; keep it
 $B679 POP HL        ; hit box offset
 $B67A ADD HL,DE     ; plus the position
 $B67B EX DE,HL      ;
 $B67C POP BC        ; hit box far corner
 $B67D ADD HL,BC     ;
 $B67E LD B,H        ; BC = far corner of the box
 $B67F LD C,L        ;
 $B680 LD IX,$B687   ; continue after the test
 $B684 JP $A85F      ; compare the box with the monk's (#R$A851 without its first half)
